* TR-1um IP62 RF inductor overlay -- generic pi model.
*
* There is no spiral inductor device in the baseline PDK.  This file provides
* a two-port pi model that the geometry generator fills in:
*
*   flow/scripts/gen_inductor_model.py --turns 4 --d-out 250 --width 8
*
* The generator computes L (Wheeler), Rdc (M2 sheet resistance), Cox (M2 to
* substrate through the stackup) and emits a ready-to-use subckt with numeric
* values.  IND_PI is the template.
*
* Topology:
*
*   p --+--[L]--[Rdc]--+-- n
*       |              |
*     [Cox1]         [Cox2]
*       |              |
*     [Rsub1]        [Rsub2]
*       |              |
*      sub            sub
*
* WARNING -- ENGINEERING ONLY
*   The stackup (libs.tech/parasitics/TR10_stackup.xml) is a placeholder:
*   dielectric thickness, substrate conductivity and via resistance are not
*   foundry-qualified.  Rsub/Csub are engineering defaults.  L is a Wheeler
*   estimate, not FastHenry/measured.  Do not quote Q as silicon data.
*
* Usage:
*   XL1 p n sub IND_PI l_nh=6.1 r_dc=12.4 c_ox=0.12p r_sub=500 c_sub=0.05p

.subckt IND_PI p n sub
.param l_nh=5 r_dc=10 c_ox=0.1p r_sub=500 c_sub=0.05p
L1 p nmid 'l_nh*1e-9'
Rdc nmid n 'r_dc'
Cox1 p ns1 'c_ox'
Rsub1 ns1 sub 'r_sub'
Cox2 n ns2 'c_ox'
Rsub2 ns2 sub 'r_sub'
Csub1 p sub 'c_sub'
Csub2 n sub 'c_sub'
.ends IND_PI
